# Purpose
Help a person ask the org brain directly, correct a draft without sending
partial edits, read earlier answers and understand what is shared.

# Source Review
Rewrite-only from the Brain Talk browser and terminal interfaces and the
existing public org brain concept. Source risk: implementation and private
chat behavior. Reuse only reader-visible controls, validation, retention
limits and source meaning. Exclude routes, tokens, capabilities, hosts,
private repository names, configuration variables and deployment details.

# Publication Gate
Feature-branch draft. Do not publish browser-specific instructions before
the matching browser behavior is verified and released. The maintainer must
check labels and limits against the final implementation. Backend source
retrieval or restart changes are not documented as shipped without evidence.

# Gotchas
- Org + general and Organisation only keep web tools off. Org + web sends only the current question to public research, then can
  synthesize with accessible org context and private conversation. Legacy
  Public web excludes org records and earlier messages. Do not imply it
  redacts private text the person types, or enables disabled model access.
- Terminal /web is one request; the next ordinary question uses the default
  org-and-general mode. Unsupported web requests must not silently change mode.
- Browser scope stays selected through Clear until changed or the view closes;
  its pending reply and answer retain the scope captured at submit.
- The visible browser transcript is bounded. The brain separately remembers
  answered private exchanges for follow-up context; Clear and Close do not
  mean Forget. Explain that boundary before suggesting private recall.
- A private chat is distinct from a note explicitly saved to the org brain;
  notes are shared with the organisation and only their author can replace
  or delete them.
- The terminal has command controls the browser may not expose. Keep each
  surface's instructions separate and verify the actual browser entry point.
- Model answers depend on the organisation's configuration. New brains can
  remain model-disabled; never imply one organisation's model binding is
  available to another.
- A missing source or an empty live board does not prove no work happened.
- Sources contains returned records matched to citations. Unverified citations
  have no matching returned record; Retrieved notes were returned without
  citations. Coverage not reported means no usable coverage details arrived.
  None of these labels independently verifies the answer's claims.
- Do not claim this change was tested on a person's physical phone unless
  that check was observed.

# Sanitization
Written fresh for a public reader. No private excerpts or deployment steps.
Final prose and links require the repository's publication checklist.

